; ============================================================
;  ARMOR MAG POUCHES - the rig every new stalker starts with
;
;  WHERE THIS PLUGS IN
;  -------------------
;  `G.A.M.M.A. Starting Loadouts` owns the new game kit, in
;  configs/items/settings/new_game_loadouts.ltx. Its shape is:
;
;      [points]                 the budget
;      [custom]                 always offered to pick from
;      [shared]:custom          everybody gets these
;      [<faction>_loadout]:shared
;
;      item_section = <pick>, <amount>, <points> [, <difficulty>]
;
;  <pick> false means the item is simply IN the new character's
;  inventory; true means it appears in the pick list at that cost in
;  points. Zero points and false is a free item, which is what the
;  starting bandage and knife are.
;
;  WHY FREE, AND WHY THIS RIG
;  --------------------------
;  With this mod on, an armour grants no magazine pockets at all - they
;  all come from a chest rig. A new character with no rig therefore has
;  NOWHERE to put a loadout magazine, which is not a difficulty choice,
;  it is a broken start. The bandolier is the smallest rig in the table
;  (2 small, 1 medium) and the cheapest to craft, so it is the honest
;  floor rather than a gift.
;
;  WHY EVERY FACTION AND NOT JUST [shared]
;  ---------------------------------------
;  [shared] would be one line instead of thirteen, and it is the wrong
;  one. A section written `[child]:parent` is filled in when the engine
;  READS that header - it copies the parent's lines as they stand at
;  that moment - so a line this file adds to [shared] afterwards never
;  reaches the faction sections that inherited from it. Both mods in
;  this install that add to the new game kit (Body Health System
;  Realistic Overhaul, and the UDP-9 file the Starting Loadouts mod
;  ships itself) write out every faction for exactly this reason. The
;  list below is the thirteen sections in the file as it stands; if a
;  future GAMMA adds a faction, its new stalkers start rigless and the
;  fix is one more block here.
;
;  ! IS THE OVERRIDE MARKER. These are the Starting Loadouts mod's
;  sections, not ours, and a second plain declaration of a foreign
;  section is a FATAL error at startup - the same rule the loot tables
;  learned the hard way. The file name matters too: DLTX only merges a
;  file called mod_<original name>_<tag>.ltx, sitting beside the
;  original.
; ============================================================

